MODIFIED FILES AND PLACEMENT INSTRUCTIONS
------------------------------------------

The following files were modified and placed in the correct directories within the Xinu source tree:

1. system/swait.c
   -> Place in: <xinu-root>/system/swait.c
   -> Implements the swait() system call (simultaneous wait on two semaphores)

2. system/ssignal.c
   -> Place in: <xinu-root>/system/ssignal.c
   -> Implements the ssignal() system call (simultaneous signal on two semaphores)

3. shell/xsh_dine.c
   -> Place in: <xinu-root>/shell/xsh_dine.c   <-- NOTE: shell/ NOT system/
   -> Modified from the provided template to seed the random number generator
      using clktime so that each run of the 'dine' command produces different
      think/eat times.

MODIFIED SUPPORTING FILES (included because they were changed):
---------------------------------------------------------------

File            Path in Xinu tree              Why changed
-----------     ----------------------------   ----------------------------------------
xsh_dine.c      shell/xsh_dine.c               Added srand(clktime) to seed RNG
lfscreate.c     device/lfs/lfscreate.c         Removed duplicate Lf_data (build fix)
xsh_ls.c        shell/xsh_ls.c                 Removed duplicate Lf_data (build fix)
xsh_mklfs.c     shell/xsh_mklfs.c              Removed duplicate Lf_data (build fix)

Note on Lf_data fix: The variable 'struct lfdata Lf_data' was defined (not just
declared) in four files: lfsinit.c, lfscreate.c, xsh_ls.c, and xsh_mklfs.c.
This caused a "multiple definition" linker error. The definition was kept only
in lfsinit.c (the correct location). The other three files use the extern
declaration already present in include/lfilesys.h.

NOTE: swait.c and ssignal.c go in system/ as per the default submission
instructions. xsh_dine.c must go in shell/ -- it will NOT work if placed
in system/.


HOW TO BUILD
------------
cd <xinu-root>/compile
make

HOW TO TEST
-----------
After booting on the board, at the Xinu shell prompt:

  dine 3        -- runs dining philosophers (4 philosophers, 3 meals each)
  dine 5        -- runs with 5 meals each

Expected output: all 4 philosophers complete all meals with no deadlock.

